@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Linux Spectra transport regressions
+
+These tests use synthetic BX bytes and owned PTYs only. They never open a physical tracker. They cover fragmented probing, binary/ASCII CRC, partial/late replies, paced writes and shared deadlines, sticky desynchronization, exact reset evidence and generic serial compatibility.
+
+Run `python3 -B Testing/Spectra/run.py` from this repository. Requires Linux, CMake, a C++17 compiler and Python 3. The runner builds only this ndicapi checkout, compiles a test-only fault shim, and reports results in ignored `Testing/Spectra/audit`. Default and 1500 microsecond serial compatibility are checked independently. Do not preload the fault shim into a real device process.
+
+Full reset token acceptance alone leaves capture desynchronized; the sole command owner must still verify INIT, COMM, configuration, tool enable and TSTART before enabling the recovered acquisition. A CRC-correct BX, flush or counter increment is not recovery evidence. PTY/software success does not establish physical tracking accuracy.
